1031. Maximum Sum of Two Non-Overlapping Subarrays

Given an integer array nums and two integers firstLen and secondLen, return the maximum sum of elements in two non-overlapping subarrays with lengths firstLen and secondLen.
The array with length firstLen could occur before or after the array with length secondLen, but they have to be non-overlapping.

Explanation:

Finding the maximum firstLen window and maximum secondLen window separately doesn't work, because they may overlap.
Instead, fix one window and keep track of the best window before it.

Idea: 
Suppose the current window is the secondLen window.

AAA | BB
AAA = firstLen window
BB = secondLen window

For every position of BB, we store:
  bestFirst = Maximum sum of any firstLen window before BB
  Then, Answer = bestFirst + currentSecondWindow
  Update the maximum answer.

bestFirst: It is not the current first window. 
  It is:
    The best firstLen window seen so far.
    Update it every iteration:
    bestFirst = Math.max(bestFirst, firstSum);

Why Prefix Sum?

  To get any window sum in O(1).
  Window Sum = prefix[r+1] - prefix[l]

Why two passes?
  The answer can be:   [firstLen] ..... [secondLen]
                                    or
                       [secondLen] ..... [firstLen]

                      So solve both and take the maximum.

Algorithm
Build Prefix Sum.
Slide the second window.
Keep updating bestFirst.
ans = max(ans, bestFirst + currentSecondWindow)
Repeat by swapping the window sizes.

Code:

class Solution {
    public int maxSumTwoNoOverlap(int[] nums, int firstLen, int secondLen) {
        int n = nums.length;
        int[] prefix = new int[n+1];
        for(int i=0;i<n;i++){
            prefix[i+1]=prefix[i]+nums[i];
        }

        return Math.max(
            helper(prefix,firstLen,secondLen), helper(prefix,secondLen,firstLen)
        );
    }

    public int helper(int[] prefix , int firstLen, int secondLen){
        int bestFirst=0; int sum=0;
    	int n = prefix.length;
        for(int i=firstLen;i<n-secondLen;i++){
            int firstSum=prefix[i]-prefix[i-firstLen];
            bestFirst = Math.max(bestFirst, firstSum);

            int secondSum = prefix[i+secondLen]-prefix[i];

            sum = Math.max(sum, bestFirst+secondSum);
        }
        return sum;
    }
}
